The code takes an array input from the user and attempts to find a missing number using the XOR bitwise operator. It first reads the size of the array and its elements. Then, it XORs values in a range and XORs elements from the array to isolate the missing value before printing the result.

Time Complexity

The program takes O(n) time to read the array elements. The two subsequent loops run at most n times, executing in O(n) time. Therefore, the overall time complexity is O(n), where n is the input size. Space complexity is O(n) for storing the array elements.

Sample Output

Enter size of array : 4
Enter the Elements in array : 0 1 2 4
Missing number: 3
